Subject: [PATCH 3/3] sidebar: hover input interrupts the launcher animation

Why Firefox source must change:
  onMouseEnter/onMouseLeave return early while the launcher animates, so
  input during the animation is dropped until it settles (then reconciled).
  Aequera requires input to supersede animation (AGENTS.md: animation must
  not delay or block direct interaction).

What it changes:
  - Hover changes are honored during an animation (the popup guard stays).
  - _animateSidebarContainer measures element rects BEFORE cancelling a
    running animation. getBoundingClientRect includes the animated
    translate, so the new animation starts from the on-screen position: a
    reversal is continuous instead of jumping to the previous end state.

Depends on: 0002 (context lines).
Validation: aequera shell tests (mouse-out mid-expand reverses without
  waiting and without a positional jump); upstream browser_sidebar_animation.js
  and browser_sidebar_expand_on_hover.js green under Firefox defaults.
Upstream risk: medium; animation bookkeeping in _animateSidebarContainer.

